 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? Sure, a complementary color is one that is strongly contrasted with it in terms of brightness or color hue. For example, white is the complementary color for black. In painting, you can use a color directly opposite it in the color wheel for strong contrast. This technique is used heavily in art supplies packaging. Yes, that's right. Black is good shadow color, but you can also use deep blue or dark purple for a bolder look. You' save bit of money, and you can use white paint mixed with it if you do buy it.",
